<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The strict (release) form: cleartext is refused for every connection.
    Both backends are HTTPS in every build type, always.

    The local desktop backend is reached through whatever TLS terminator the
    rider runs (tailscale serve or an ordinary reverse proxy, both accepted;
    owner decision, #192/#260), so it needs no exception here and Step 2 adds
    none. This file is final, not provisional.

    Do not add a domain-config to this file. A strict base-config already
    permits every HTTPS host, which is exactly what lets the rider point the
    app at any hostname they like; naming one here would replace that
    flexibility with a hardcoded host and buy nothing.

    The debug build replaces this resource (same name, src/debug) with a copy
    that permits cleartext to loopback hosts only: the dev harness seen through
    the emulator. That copy cannot ship — it lives in the debug source set.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
</network-security-config>
